 Day 6 — GCP Compute Engine + MIG + Autoscaling

Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ You need to deploy stateless web servers with zero-downtime scaling. How will you design this using Instance Templates + MIG + Autoscaling?

2️⃣ Your VM workloads spike during business hours and remain idle overnight. How will you configure cost-optimized autoscaling policies?

3️⃣ A VM reboot causes app failure because local SSD data is lost. What alternative design will you implement to avoid data loss?

4️⃣ Your application needs GPU for AI inference workloads. How will you pick machine type, GPU type, and configure scheduling policies?

5️⃣ MIG instances are scaling out, but CPU stays high and latency increases. What tuning parameters, instance readiness, and scaling triggers will you analyze?

6️⃣ You need a blue-green deployment for Compute Engine. How will you achieve this using instance templates + MIG + load balancer?

7️⃣ A VM template was updated but the MIG is still running old instances. How do you roll out the new version safely?

8️⃣ You must run scheduled batch jobs only at 2 AM daily. Which instance types/pricing models will you use and why?

9️⃣ Sensitive compute workloads should run on dedicated hardware only. How will you enforce this using Sole-Tenant Nodes and placement policies?

🔟 Your startup expects unpredictable traffic spikes. Spot VMs reduce cost but must avoid downtime. How will you architect a hybrid MIG?

1️⃣1️⃣ VM boots slowly due to heavy startup scripts. How will you optimize using custom images, instance metadata, and startup ordering?

1️⃣2️⃣ A VM OS got corrupted and won’t boot. How will you recover the disk and start a replacement instance?

1️⃣3️⃣ You must migrate 300 on-prem VMs to GCP securely with minimal downtime. Which tools will you choose and how will you design cutover?

1️⃣4️⃣ A VM must auto-heal when the application becomes unresponsive, not just when OS fails. How will you configure custom health checks?

1️⃣5️⃣ Your backend service requires encrypted VM disks + snapshot backups + cross-region disaster recovery. How will you design the strategy end-to-end?

